// The shapes `#[derive(Xml)]` does not reach are refused by name, and a `Map` is the one a reader
// coming from `#[derive(Json)]` will try first: a JSON object has keys and an XML element has
// child names, and which of a map's keys becomes an element name is a schema decision.
use xml

#[derive(Xml)]
struct Bag {
    items: Map<string, int>
}

fn main() {
    print(1)
}
